        100["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Mesh files</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The compact lossless .fmsh<br />format for meshes and results<br />and its entropy coder.</div>"]
        style 100 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        101["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Fixtures and test kit</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Test meshes and the SOI wire<br />cross-section used by the<br />tests of every physics crate.</div>"]
        style 101 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        102["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Meshing facade</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>MeshPlan and mesh_model (the<br />one way to mesh a geom<br />model), the serialisable<br />request and report, sizing<br />from the physics, and the 2D<br />triangulation core.</div>"]
        style 102 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        103["<div style='font-weight: bold'>3D meshing</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The lattice tetrahedral<br />mesher on Domain3, Rivara<br />refinement, the adapter from<br />a 3D geom model, adaptive<br />meshing driven by exact<br />faces, face sizes and<br />max_dev, curved boundary<br />edges, and conformal 3D<br />sheet-stack meshing.</div>"]
        style 103 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        104["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Structured absorbing layers</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Structured PML around a<br />box-shaped or geom-model<br />mesh: prisms, hexahedra,<br />quads, labels.</div>"]
        style 104 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        105["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Meshing validation harness</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>A small independent scalar<br />Helmholtz solver with PML<br />used to validate meshes.</div>"]
        style 105 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        106["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Metric fields</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Riemannian metrics in 2D and<br />3D, metric fields, the<br />simplex working mesh and<br />per-phase timers.</div>"]
        style 106 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        107["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Adaptation operators</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Edge split, collapse, flip<br />and smoothing on the working<br />meshes in 2D and 3D, with the<br />vertex classification.</div>"]
        style 107 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        108["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Adaptation drivers</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Passes of operators until the<br />mesh conforms to the metric,<br />with geometry oracles saying<br />where a boundary vertex may<br />go.</div>"]
        style 108 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        109["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Error estimators</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Error estimation and the<br />solve-estimate-adapt loop;<br />the Maxwell residual<br />estimator for edge elements.</div>"]
        style 109 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        110["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Matrices and vectors</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The one matrix type Csr over<br />a generic scalar, block<br />storage, multivector kernels,<br />operator interfaces, dense<br />helpers, Matrix Market,<br />problem bundles and<br />test-problem generators.</div>"]
        style 110 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        111["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Linear algebra driver</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The door the physics kernels<br />use: a direct solve,<br />eigenpairs near a shift, and<br />the solver interface for<br />models.</div>"]
        style 111 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        112["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Direct solvers</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Shifted sparse direct solves<br />with symbolic reuse, LU with<br />a user ordering, block<br />low-rank factorisation, mixed<br />precision, nested dissection.</div>"]
        style 112 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        113["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Krylov solvers</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>CG, MINRES, GMRES, BiCGStab,<br />COCR, QMR, IDR(s), GCRO-DR<br />for real and complex systems.</div>"]
        style 113 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        114["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Eigensolvers</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Krylov-Schur, LOBPCG,<br />Jacobi-Davidson, quadratic<br />and nonlinear eigenproblems,<br />contour integral, Chebyshev<br />filtering, real Arnoldi for<br />the 2D modes, sensitivities.</div>"]
        style 114 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        115["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Preconditioners</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Smoothed-aggregation<br />multigrid (scalar and<br />elastic), auxiliary-space<br />Maxwell and divergence<br />solvers, Schwarz, field-split<br />and incomplete<br />factorisations.</div>"]
        style 115 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        116["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Time, nonlinear, sweeps</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Time integration, Newton and<br />optimisation, matrix<br />exponential action,<br />reduced-order frequency<br />sweeps and matrix-free<br />high-order operators.</div>"]
        style 116 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        117["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Finite-element basics</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Lagrange P1/P2 elements and<br />quadrature, the 2D<br />edge-element basis, derived<br />fields, PML coordinate<br />stretching, Floquet pairs and<br />material properties per<br />domain.</div>"]
        style 117 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        118["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Material specification</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>TOML material files with<br />explicit units, tensors,<br />dispersion models evaluated<br />at the wavelength, Zimmermann<br />BCS superconducting<br />conductivity, provenance and<br />the library loader.</div>"]
        style 118 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        119["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Optical mode sets</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Optical modes of a 2D<br />cross-section as a<br />field-evaluable set with the<br />material data to evaluate<br />them.</div>"]
        style 119 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        120["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Frame and sections</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The one place that knows the<br />wafer axes (x lateral, z<br />normal, waves along +y).</div>"]
        style 120 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        121["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Expressions</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>A small safe expression<br />evaluator for user input (a<br />copy of geom's kept equal by<br />a corpus test), and the typed<br />tree over complex field<br />values that the reductions of<br />results evaluate, and the<br />text formulas parsed into it<br />(ADR 90).</div>"]
        style 121 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        122["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Runtime services</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The shared worker pool, stage<br />log and cancel, the<br />warm-start context of the<br />shift-and-invert eigensolvers<br />(ADR 96), and refusal of NaN<br />and infinity.</div>"]
        style 122 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        99["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Mesh</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The native mixed-cell mesh,<br />the exchange mesh the physics<br />take, simplex meshes with<br />their numbering of unknowns,<br />draw-only meshes and quality<br />statistics.</div>"]
        style 99 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
      end

